            <ArticleTitle>Meeting report: a hard look at the state of enamel research.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1038/ijos.2017.40</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The Encouraging Novel Amelogenesis Models and Ex vivo cell Lines (ENAMEL) Development workshop was held on 23 June 2017 at the Bethesda headquarters of the National Institute of Dental and Craniofacial Research (NIDCR). Discussion topics included model organisms, stem cells/cell lines, and tissues/3D cell culture/organoids. Scientists from a number of disciplines, representing institutions from across the United States, gathered to discuss advances in our understanding of enamel, as well as future directions for the field.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
